    {
     "id": "lcd-ili9342e",
     "text": "Units made from 2026.8.7 carry an ILI9342E LCD driver instead of the ILI9342C. Programs that use M5GFX need M5GFX 0.2.27 or later on those units; older builds may show a blank or wrong display.",
     "src": [
      "m5-cores3"
     ],
     "confidence": "high",
     "last_verified": "2026-10-03"
    },
    {
     "id": "m5-pio-devkitc",
     "text": "M5's own PlatformIO example for CoreS3 does not use the m5stack-cores3 board id. It sets platform = espressif32@6.7.0, board = esp32-s3-devkitc-1 and the build flags -DESP32S3, -DBOARD_HAS_PSRAM, -mfix-esp32-psram-cache-issue, -DARDUINO_USB_CDC_ON_BOOT=1 and -DARDUINO_USB_MODE=1 (its debug level and upload speed are left out here). platform-espressif32 first shipped m5stack-cores3 in 6.4.0; a platform older than 6.4.0 reports it as an unknown board.",
     "src": [
      "m5-cores3",
      "pio-esp32",
      "pio-esp32-cores3"
